    <x:String x:Key="Diag_ResolveIdeviceWin">Place idevice_id.exe into the 'idevice-tools' directory or install libimobiledevice for Windows.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Diag_ResolveIdeviceMac">Run: 'brew install libimobiledevice' in Terminal.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Diag_ResolveIdeviceLinux">Run: 'sudo apt-get install libimobiledevice-utils' in Terminal.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Diag_ResolveIdeviceinfo">Ensure the complete libimobiledevice suite is installed.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Diag_ResolveAdbWin">Install Android SDK Platform-Tools or copy adb.exe to the idevice-tools directory.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Diag_ResolveAdbMac">Run: 'brew install android-platform-tools' in Terminal.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Diag_ResolveAdbLinux">Run: 'sudo apt-get install adb' in Terminal.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Diag_ResolveTunnel">Install the tunnel connector, or place cloudflared in the 'idevice-tools' directory.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Diag_ResolveUsbmuxdPortable">Start the portable usbmuxd background daemon.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Diag_ResolveAppleService">Download and install the lightweight Apple driver and the usbmuxd daemon.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Diag_ResolveUsbmuxdMac">Make sure usbmuxd is running, or restart the computer.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Diag_ResolveUsbmuxdLinux">Run: 'sudo systemctl start usbmuxd' or 'sudo usbmuxd -f -v'.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Diag_ResolveUsbCable">Check the USB cable, try another USB port directly on the computer (not a hub), unlock the phone and tap 'Trust' if asked.</x:String>

